.th MKDIR I 3/15/72
.sh NAME
mkdir  \*-  make a directory
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd mkdir
dirname ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Mkdir
creates specified directories
in mode 775.
The standard entries `\fB.\fR' and `\fB..\fR' are made automatically.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
rmdir (I), mknod (II)
.sh BUGS
.it Mkdir
must be a set-super-user-id program.  Consequently it cannot
know your real user id if you have used
.it su
(I) to become the super-user, and any directory it then creates
will be owned by root.
